IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P9-gate`
IMPORT `P9-art-85-87`

-- Tests for Articles 85, 86 and 87. Expected values are written from the text of the Articles, Article 113 (group General
-- from 2 August 2026) and Article 111(2), never copied from the encoding's own output.

§ `The AI systems the tests use`

`the new Annex III system` MEANS `AI system` WITH
    `date placed on the market or put into service` IS Date 1 1 2030
    `route` IS `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III`
    `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS FALSE

`the legacy Annex III system` MEANS `AI system` WITH
    `date placed on the market or put into service` IS Date 1 1 2027
    `route` IS `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III`
    `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS FALSE

`the Annex I system` MEANS `AI system` WITH
    `date placed on the market or put into service` IS Date 1 1 2030
    `route` IS `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I`
    `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS FALSE

`the system that is not high-risk` MEANS `AI system` WITH
    `date placed on the market or put into service` IS Date 1 1 2020
    `route` IS `Route neither`
    `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS FALSE

§ `Article 85(1)`

-- args: date asked, the person is a natural or legal person, the person has grounds to consider that there has been an infringement
#ASSERT `Art 85(1) the person may submit a complaint to the relevant market surveillance authority` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 85(1) the person may submit a complaint to the relevant market surveillance authority` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 85(1) the person may submit a complaint to the relevant market surveillance authority` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 85(1) the person may submit a complaint to the relevant market surveillance authority` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 85(1) the person may submit a complaint to the relevant market surveillance authority` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the rule holds on each side of 27 July 2026 (the Omnibus): before 2 August 2026 nothing, after it the right
#ASSERT `Art 85(1) the person may submit a complaint to the relevant market surveillance authority` (Date 26 7 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 85(1) the person may submit a complaint to the relevant market surveillance authority` (Date 28 7 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 85(1) the person may submit a complaint to the relevant market surveillance authority` (Date 3 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Article 85(2)`

-- args: date asked, a complaint has been submitted under Article 85(1)
#ASSERT `Art 85(2) the market surveillance authority must take the complaint into account and handle it in line with the dedicated procedures` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 85(2) the market surveillance authority must take the complaint into account and handle it in line with the dedicated procedures` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 85(2) the market surveillance authority must take the complaint into account and handle it in line with the dedicated procedures` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 85(2) the duty of the market surveillance authority to take the complaint into account` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 85 the market surveillance authority` DOES `Art 85(2) take the complaint into account for the purpose of conducting market surveillance activities and handle it in line with the dedicated procedures` AT 5
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 85(2) the duty of the market surveillance authority to take the complaint into account` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 400

§ `Article 86`

-- args: date asked, system, affected person subject to a decision, decision taken by the deployer on the output of the system, listed in Annex III under a point other than 2, listed under point 2, the decision has legal or similarly significant effects, the person considers it has an adverse impact, an exception or restriction under Union or national law, the right is otherwise provided for under Union law
-- Before the group applies (1 August 2026): NOTHING. From 2 August 2026, with every element met: JUST TRUE.
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the affected person has the right to obtain from the deployer clear and meaningful explanations` (Date 1 8 2026) `the new Annex III system` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the affected person has the right to obtain from the deployer clear and meaningful explanations` (Date 2 8 2026) `the new Annex III system` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Each element missing, in turn: NOTHING (a grant limited by its own wording).
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the affected person has the right to obtain from the deployer clear and meaningful explanations` (Date 2 8 2026) `the new Annex III system` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the affected person has the right to obtain from the deployer clear and meaningful explanations` (Date 2 8 2026) `the new Annex III system` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the affected person has the right to obtain from the deployer clear and meaningful explanations` (Date 2 8 2026) `the new Annex III system` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the affected person has the right to obtain from the deployer clear and meaningful explanations` (Date 2 8 2026) `the new Annex III system` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the affected person has the right to obtain from the deployer clear and meaningful explanations` (Date 2 8 2026) `the new Annex III system` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The exception for point 2 (and the written "with the exception of systems listed under point 2"): the text says no.
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the affected person has the right to obtain from the deployer clear and meaningful explanations` (Date 2 8 2026) `the new Annex III system` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Paragraph 2: an exception or restriction under Union or national law: the text says no.
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the affected person has the right to obtain from the deployer clear and meaningful explanations` (Date 2 8 2026) `the new Annex III system` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Paragraph 3: the right otherwise provided for under Union law: the text says no ("only to the extent").
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the affected person has the right to obtain from the deployer clear and meaningful explanations` (Date 2 8 2026) `the new Annex III system` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Both paragraph 2 and paragraph 3 apply: each says no, so the answer is JUST FALSE.
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the affected person has the right to obtain from the deployer clear and meaningful explanations` (Date 2 8 2026) `the new Annex III system` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An AI system that is not listed in Annex III (Annex I route, or not high-risk): the Article is silent.
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the affected person has the right to obtain from the deployer clear and meaningful explanations` (Date 2 8 2026) `the Annex I system` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the affected person has the right to obtain from the deployer clear and meaningful explanations` (Date 2 8 2026) `the system that is not high-risk` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Article 111(2): a legacy Annex III system placed on 1 January 2027 and not changed is saved: NOTHING; changed it would be covered (tested in the Art 80 tests).
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the affected person has the right to obtain from the deployer clear and meaningful explanations` (Date 2 8 2028) `the legacy Annex III system` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The deployer's duty is the same relation seen from the deployer: same arguments, same answers (mirror).
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the deployer must give the affected person clear and meaningful explanations` (Date 1 8 2026) `the new Annex III system` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the deployer must give the affected person clear and meaningful explanations` (Date 2 8 2026) `the new Annex III system` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the deployer must give the affected person clear and meaningful explanations` (Date 2 8 2026) `the new Annex III system` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the deployer must give the affected person clear and meaningful explanations` (Date 2 8 2026) `the new Annex III system` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the deployer must give the affected person clear and meaningful explanations` (Date 2 8 2026) `the new Annex III system` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 86(1) the duty of the deployer to give the affected person clear and meaningful explanations` (Date 2 8 2026) `the new Annex III system` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 86 the deployer` DOES `Art 86(1) give the affected person clear and meaningful explanations of the role of the AI system in the decision-making procedure and the main elements of the decision taken` AT 5
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 86(1) the duty of the deployer to give the affected person clear and meaningful explanations` (Date 2 8 2026) `the new Annex III system` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 400

-- What the explanation covers.
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the explanation is within the right` `Art 86(1) the role of the AI system in the decision-making procedure` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the explanation is within the right` `Art 86(1) the main elements of the decision taken` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 86(1) the explanation is within the right` `Art 86(1) another explanation` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Article 87`

-- args: date asked, the matter is the reporting of an infringement of this Regulation or the protection of a person reporting one
#ASSERT `Art 87 Directive (EU) 2019/1937 applies to the matter` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 87 Directive (EU) 2019/1937 applies to the matter` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 87 Directive (EU) 2019/1937 applies to the matter` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
